<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top</id><updated>2026-08-31T05:49:23Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-top" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>US: Deadly flash flood hits Grand Canyon</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2452647af825f94ea35d81423eea572da80ca6e2d02ca84b18a44cc45cb1849e</id><updated>2026-08-31T05:49:13Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T05:28:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-deadly-flash-flood-hits-grand-canyon/a-78568246--8e288eaefe40.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-deadly-flash-flood-hits-grand-canyon/a-78568246?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Arizona's Grand Canyon received rainfall of up to 1 inch triggering a flash flood which forced more than 60 people to evacuate. At least one person has died, with over a dozen missing.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Google Maps changes Lake Ontario to 'Lake America' in US</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ec02d39a06475815efc77fb7695a7c3f439463cf4d90779cc559c215a5024c3c</id><updated>2026-08-31T05:49:16Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T03:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/google-maps-changes-lake-ontario-to-lake-america-in-us/a-78567904--36bfb91c3e9c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/google-maps-changes-lake-ontario-to-lake-america-in-us/a-78567904?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The name change even made its way to some government websites in Canada which pull map data from Google Maps. Meanwhile, Ontario Premier Doug Ford made his position clear by erecting a billboard on the shore of the lake.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Iran war: US military strikes Iran's Larak Island</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:998c39bf708cc12861cdfd27728dc735c502716e1f797d7a6e04b3c32d9fd082</id><updated>2026-08-31T05:49:19Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T00:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-war-us-military-strikes-iran-s-larak-island/live-78566992--c647887e8c6d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-war-us-military-strikes-iran-s-larak-island/live-78566992?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The attack was the first in over a month. Iran's Revolutionary Guard said they targeted Jordan in retaliation, with Iranian media reporting the UAE was also attacked. DW has the latest.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Fact check: Germany's Merz misstates record in ARD interview</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:863d8c178a2457ad938641d8ee77b12740b0234b9d9029f269033b9bb3414076</id><updated>2026-08-31T05:49:23Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T19:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/fact-check-germany-s-merz-misstates-record-in-ard-interview/a-78566319--dfc2a1b2209b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/fact-check-germany-s-merz-misstates-record-in-ard-interview/a-78566319?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Migration, debt and electric vehicles: Chancellor Friedrich Merz made several misleading claims in his ARD summer interview. DW Fact check reviewed them live.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Merz warns of 'problems' in Saxony-Anhalt under AfD</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8d23428bc1937f59e92e86be71746606ced0ff898f61f23b5b2b7cfb6d53daf7</id><updated>2026-08-31T05:48:04Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T18:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-merz-warns-of-problems-in-saxony-anhalt-under-afd/live-78555302--ce8222193763.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-merz-warns-of-problems-in-saxony-anhalt-under-afd/live-78555302?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Chancellor Friedrich Merz said that a victory for the far-right Alternative for Germany (AfD) party in next week's election in Saxony-Anhalt would seriously damage the eastern German state.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>NASA launches first telescope named after female scientist</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:60a1122e1455ab9378f30c24022c2c0a5cc3a95a9c4b8ee252a12eba321c7304</id><updated>2026-08-31T05:48:04Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T16:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nasa-launches-first-telescope-named-after-female-scientist/a-78565941--a093597a353c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nasa-launches-first-telescope-named-after-female-scientist/a-78565941?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Nancy Grace Roman Space Telescope, named after NASA's first Chief of Astronomy, will observe black holes, exoplanets and exploding stars.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's Christian Churches take a stand against far right</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e3200271ab1cc778010ed046d8e2bea889d0a3ba27147f58a1a8c61f63ccb00d</id><updated>2026-08-31T05:48:04Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T15:56:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-christian-churches-take-a-stand-against-far-right/a-78482465--df145112005e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-christian-churches-take-a-stand-against-far-right/a-78482465?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The AfD in Saxony-Anhalt has embarked on a confrontational course toward the churches. Representatives of the Catholic and Protestant churches are responding with a mix of anxiety and resolve.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>EU wants drones to spray pesticides, but it could backfire</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1aecd5e35b46eaf88d4cce77600ccb3032c758d65d620d7ec3112d8d2e7cbd0c</id><updated>2026-08-31T05:48:04Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T15:11:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-wants-drones-to-spray-pesticides-but-it-could-backfire/a-78557154--0a305cd9a870.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-wants-drones-to-spray-pesticides-but-it-could-backfire/a-78557154?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The EU wants to lift a decades-old ban on spraying pesticides from the air, allowing drones to be used for greater precision. But experts warn the plan could lead to even more pesticides being used in agriculture.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>Guinea-Bissau votes to reshape presidency</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:71b73bdd3875ce6215f0c2db45f30ac7d649f9498910a2466a080d9eb923178f</id><updated>2026-08-31T05:48:04Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T12:01:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/guinea-bissau-votes-to-reshape-presidency/a-78562523--3b8aa87de3b8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/guinea-bissau-votes-to-reshape-presidency/a-78562523?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The West African nation's military government wants to amend the constitution to give more powers to the president. The junta, which seized power last year, says it will hold elections in December.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Ferry carrying over 260 people capsizes off Cyprus</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:830ed2c681ca4690b45474857b950116d890d5ac6dd5f4b7a31611c8c14dd8cc</id><updated>2026-08-31T05:48:04Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T11:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ferry-carrying-over-260-people-capsizes-off-cyprus/a-78562769--e475f04f9878.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ferry-carrying-over-260-people-capsizes-off-cyprus/a-78562769?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Several people have died after a passenger ⁠boat carrying more than 260 people capsized off ‌northern Cyprus. ‌</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Iceland voters reject EU accession talks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:32b876f926ac14a158ea4f24034d8b912b14eb712ef4fd6a86676b76cfeb5804</id><updated>2026-08-31T05:48:04Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T10:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iceland-voters-reject-eu-accession-talks/a-78560633--a28445d5d605.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iceland-voters-reject-eu-accession-talks/a-78560633?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A nationwide referendum failed to win enough support to restart negotiations on European Union membership, despite geopolitical tensions in the North Atlantic.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Greece, Turkey clash over protected Aegean marine areas</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:924f392d7c6411f09c6b905145557b6c6916e354d539cb14c0625527d4bd1fd4</id><updated>2026-08-31T05:48:04Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T09:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/greece-turkey-clash-over-protected-aegean-marine-areas/a-78550021--5945932eb9fb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/greece-turkey-clash-over-protected-aegean-marine-areas/a-78550021?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Turkey has announced the creation of two protected zones in a disputed area of the Aegean Sea, sparking an angry reaction from Greece. Does this mark a new chapter in a long-running dispute between the two countries?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>India's citizen-led school audits test limits of activism</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:330885bd4f23adffe5c3b14e1fd79f695d559f65de2bfbaa498357aa1e27d0d5</id><updated>2026-08-31T05:48:04Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T09:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-s-citizen-led-school-audits-test-limits-of-activism/a-78545789--626068e76fe6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-s-citizen-led-school-audits-test-limits-of-activism/a-78545789?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The student-led "Cockroach" movement is taking its campaign for accountability to government schools, but the activists' methods are encountering growing resistance from authorities.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Manhunt underway after woman killed in Swiss rave shooting</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d067170cdda4baa133772e8919754a4557e101a4d25a8a3dfa8257b4bd43bbe8</id><updated>2026-08-31T05:48:04Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T08:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/manhunt-underway-after-woman-killed-in-swiss-rave-shooting/a-78561106--973b52137dfd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/manhunt-underway-after-woman-killed-in-swiss-rave-shooting/a-78561106?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The shooting at a rave in the northern Swiss town of Aarau, near Zürich, left at least one person dead and five wounded. Police said they were still searching for the perpetrator or perpetrators.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Nepal issues fresh flood warning as 3,000 still missing</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ca7e04dcea83211c05bf219a77524829e117728c2ade503b4c79e0105aa8d765</id><updated>2026-08-31T05:48:04Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T06:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nepal-issues-fresh-flood-warning-as-3-000-still-missing/a-78561068--3def83ade1cc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nepal-issues-fresh-flood-warning-as-3-000-still-missing/a-78561068?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Rescuers are trying to reach dozens of hydropower workers trapped in flooded tunnels, but have been hampered by further rainfall.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Norway’s new King Haakon remembers ‘dear father’ Harald in first speech as sovereign</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:325a427f74be41aea72afef181f7a772b1b73a52e2731ef1d3cd4178a5956465</id><updated>2026-08-31T05:48:04Z</updated><published>2026-08-29T22:22:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/norway-s-new-king-haakon-remembers-dear-father-harald-in-first-speech-as-sovereign/a-78560155--02c54a032890.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/norway-s-new-king-haakon-remembers-dear-father-harald-in-first-speech-as-sovereign/a-78560155?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">New monarch Haakon VIII paid an emotional tribute to his late father, Harald V, in his first address to the nation. Vowing to follow his own path, Haakon pledged to uphold Norway’s democracy, unity and inclusive values.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Turkish, Somali forces free vessel seized by pirates in Somalia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e5a3b99fd4acb8bb9b969ffd92e89a10e55a196832237828e57813932ee85e98</id><updated>2026-08-31T05:48:04Z</updated><published>2026-08-29T20:54:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/turkish-somali-forces-free-vessel-seized-by-pirates-in-somalia/a-78560087--0908c6599c56.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/turkish-somali-forces-free-vessel-seized-by-pirates-in-somalia/a-78560087?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Turkish and Somali forces have freed the MV LUTUF after pirates hijacked the vessel off the coast of Somalia. The 10-day operation killed 14 alleged pirates and destroyed four boats used by the attackers.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Israeli settlers attack Palestinian homes in West Bank</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:17377eb60222a3bf6476e36d657872aa09612089ef020836752cb2bff2a62d49</id><updated>2026-08-31T05:48:04Z</updated><published>2026-08-29T19:56:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/israeli-settlers-attack-palestinian-homes-in-west-bank/a-78560116--06b00ccd6355.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/israeli-settlers-attack-palestinian-homes-in-west-bank/a-78560116?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Masked Israeli settlers launched their first major attack since initiating a siege in the village of Qusra earlier this month. Saturday's attacks were met with rare criticism from Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Zimbabwe crash involving church minibus kills 27</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:678c96b645be9c4b72dc2a26eb649eb49b5ee2de832d1a9fcd72363372315101</id><updated>2026-08-31T05:48:04Z</updated><published>2026-08-29T17:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/zimbabwe-crash-involving-church-minibus-kills-27/a-78558710--4749bd5c44e7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/zimbabwe-crash-involving-church-minibus-kills-27/a-78558710?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Dozens of people were killed when a minibus carrying churchgoers collided head-on with a truck in central Zimbabwe. The crash near the town of Chivhu is the latest deadly road accident in the African country.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Russian-American heads Trump's planned Caucasus trade route</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d84347910af97c7b7d32bc6659ece1e237f8c378a506d4823758cdbcdebb163a</id><updated>2026-08-31T05:48:04Z</updated><published>2026-08-29T16:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russian-american-heads-trump-s-planned-caucasus-trade-route/a-78547064--e5f93782e76f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russian-american-heads-trump-s-planned-caucasus-trade-route/a-78547064?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A Russian-born businessman heads the investment fund financing the so-called "Trump Route," a planned corridor through Armenia linking Azerbaijan with Nakhchivan. Who is Konstantin Sokolov, and what role does he play?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Saxony-Anhalt election: Why the AfD is so strong</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7df601728548cbed4a8170283b57456f277092e9a8bacfd84f542845a0caf522</id><updated>2026-08-31T05:48:04Z</updated><published>2026-08-29T16:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/saxony-anhalt-election-why-the-afd-is-so-strong/a-78482588--e5ea6817c869.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/saxony-anhalt-election-why-the-afd-is-so-strong/a-78482588?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The AfD is polling above 40% ahead of Saxony-Anhalt's election on September 6. What is driving support for the far right in this predominantly rural eastern German state?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry></feed>
